rted nonempty text identity X.", "Register an ordinary empty mapping as X, with no extra block or concurrent mutation; registration returns normally.", "Direct generic trigger of X with no args; separate menu function consumer is not used."], "normal_control": "Register a normal callable for X whose result is 7, then generic trigger normally returns 7 without prepending X. Trigger an unregistered identity normally returns no value.", "minimal_counterexample": "The ordinary mapping is accepted and retained at X, but direct trigger tries to invoke it as a callback. Because an ordinary mapping has no callable operation, a missing-call error propagates; no normal result is produced. The stored mapping remains registered.", "outcomes": {"normal": "Callable handler returns its result; absent handler returns no value.", "cancel": "There is no confirmation or cancellation interaction at these primitive entries.", "failure": "Accepted noncallable mapping fails at invocation, not registration; no local catch converts it to empty/false.", "partial_commit": "Registration has already stored X. Failed triggering does not remove it or roll back earlier external state; no mapping effect was invoked."}, "necessary_consumers": ["MenuHandlers.add accepts option mappings through the same identity-handler registry.", "MenuHandlers.call retrieves a mapping and invokes its selected named function, so a mapping with effect callback remains a valid menu option.", "Content-key variants use the same accepted-shape check and invoke resolved values as callbacks, so the same callable scope should be made explicit if their trigger contract is expanded."], "negative_evidence": {"scope": "All Markdown under deliverables/final-specification-set searched; WP05 full1–147 and kernel catalog full1–288 continuously read. Global search is locator evidence, not global read credit.", "logs": ["logs/hash_negative_search.stdout", "logs/hash_negative_relevant.stdout", "logs/hash_negative_final.stdout", "logs/h