ectory and no fallback path is requested.", "minimal_counterexample": {"given": "F8 edge, working directory A, host data directory B distinct from A, primary Screenshots directory writable, screenshot request normally returns.", "source_result": "The request targets A/Screenshots with a wall-clock date/time-to-millisecond PNG basename, rather than B. After a primary directory/write failure, the same basename is requested beneath B instead.", "contract_gap": "WP17 only states that F8 triggers a screenshot. The accurate WP65 help label says same folder as save but is explicitly content, and cannot determine this actual two-stage path workflow."}, "normal_cancel_failure_partial_commit": {"normal": "Name a .png from the current wall-clock fields, ensure the relative Screenshots directory and request the primary capture.", "cancel": "There is no interactive confirmation/cancel operation in this helper; absence of the F8 edge does not request it.", "primary_failure": "Directory setup or primary capture failure enters the fallback and requests the same basename via the host data-directory filename resolver.", "fallback_failure": "A fallback failure escapes this helper; later completion sound request is not reached.", "partial_commit": "Any already-created directory or successfully requested screenshot has no source rollback; a later completion-sound failure does not imply file rollback. Millisecond filename granularity does not prove uniqueness.", "sound": "Only after normally returning capture does the helper conditionally request the named completion sound when its resource check succeeds; actual audio is unknown."}, "necessary_consumers": [{"path": "Data/Scripts/001_Technical/004_Input.rb", "lines": [17, 20], "clause": "Default F8 caller"}, {"path": "Data/Scripts/001_Technical/002_Files/001_FileTests.rb", "lines": [244, 256], "clause": "Fallback basename to host data-directory resolver"}], "negative_evidence": {"scope": "All Markdown files beneath deliverables/final-spe